OPEN MATHEMATICAL RISKS (NOT MISREPRESENTED AS PROVED RESULTS)
=============================================================
1. No finite univalent Weber--Airy--endpoint chain, progressive paths, sheet
   exchange, or uniform overlap estimates have been constructed.  Therefore
   C_ess=0 and the Fedoryuk contraction are conjectural connection mechanisms.
2. The eta^(2/3), constant, and eta^(-2/3) fixed-level coefficients are
   strongly checked formal operator coefficients, but no global remainder
   theorem identifies the whole series with exact eigenvalues.  There is no
   uniformity for n growing with eta.
3. The local multiplicative weak-drive representation has poles at zeros of
   its leading 0F1 factor; no canonical-product/global Bargmann closure is
   established.
4. Iteration figures use strong numerical interventions and, for eta=0.25,
   an explicitly out-of-regime extrapolation.  They are evidence only for the
   regularized plotted map.

